<title>USA: Capitol Multimedia says sells assets to CUC unit.</title>
<headline>Capitol Multimedia says sells assets to CUC unit.</headline>
<dateline>CONCORD, Mass. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Capitol Multimedia Inc said Friday it sold selected multimedia assets to Davidson &amp; Associates Inc, a division of CUC International Inc for about $2.5 million in cash.</p>
<p>The company said the assets include art, animation and audio production capabilities located in St. Petersburg, Russia, and Concord, Mass.</p>
<p>The company said it has retained all rights to its 14 multimedia CD-ROM products on the market, three new CD-ROM titles near completion, all CD-I products, all software tools and engines, and software development capabilities in the U.S. and Russia.</p>
</text>
